# Living docs (source control log, Features, bug journal)

After finishing work that changes **product behavior**, **architecture**, or **known bugs/fixes**, update the matching docs in the same turn (do not wait for the user to ask).

| Doc | Update when |
|-----|-------------|
| `docs/source control log.md` | User-visible or ship-relevant change (feature, fix, migration, catalog, launch path). Add a dated bullet under **Updates**; adjust **Focus** / **Minimum** if release criteria changed. |
| `docs/Features and Inner Workings.md` | Behavior or implementation map changed (tabs, launch pipeline, emulators, streaming, data model, pitfalls). Edit the relevant section; keep “how it works today” accurate. |
| `docs/bug journal.md` | A bug was diagnosed or fixed. Add/update a **BJ-###** entry (symptom / cause / fix / commit or *in progress*). |

## Skip when

- Pure refactors with no behavior change, typos-only, or experiments that will be reverted.
- Doc-only edits that already are the update.

## Style

- Match each file’s existing voice and structure (short bullets in the source control log; handbook sections in Features; table rows in the bug journal).
- Prefer **why** and **where in code**; link related BJ / Features sections when helpful.
- Mark uncommitted work **in progress**.
